{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n\n`test_the_installed_pandoc_matches_the_legacy_fixture_provenance` fails on every arm64 macOS\nhost that has a working pandoc configured:\n\n```\nValueError: Pandoc binary SHA-256 mismatch for darwin-arm64:\n  expected  d7b1e75cd20ee6a788a1399492be07d4559949e18e55f34cfc5c91807fdfa90d\n  installed 140353e19f2518a76aa144ce90a7afcb6f485ba94d0dbe069e77c805277908c3\n```\n\n- Failing test: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_the_installed_pandoc_matches_the_legacy_fixture_provenance`\n- Fails at `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py:476`\n- Raised from `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py:149-152`\n- Expectation frozen at `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py:60-63`\n\n## Root cause — confirmed by measurement, not inference (re-checked 2026-10-20 on origin/main c0cf1022671)\n\nThe `darwin-arm64` entry pins the SHA-256 of an **x86_64** binary.\n\n```\n$ file .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pypandoc/files/pandoc\nMach-O 64-bit executable x86_64\n$ shasum -a 256 .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pypandoc/files/pandoc\nd7b1e75cd20ee6a788a1399492be07d4559949e18e55f34cfc5c91807fdfa90d\n```\n\nThat is byte-for-byte the value pinned under the `darwin-arm64` key.\n\nThe provenance table is:\n\n```python\nSUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256 = {\n    \"darwin-arm64\": \"d7b1e75cd20ee6a788a1399492be07d4559949e18e55f34cfc5c91807fdfa90d\",\n    \"linux-x86_64\": \"decd3dd11a3fe0c16ce56443343ec53adde6fbed6f97d7f56f06b1c424248e7b\",\n}\n```\n\nThe platform key is derived from the **host** via `stable_platform_key(system, machine)`, while\nthe hashed bytes came from the `pypandoc-binary==1.17` wheel payload. That wheel advertises\n`macosx_11_0_arm64` but ships an x86_64 executable, so on an arm64 host the key says\n`darwin-arm64` and the value is an x86_64 binary's hash.\n\nThe introducing commit `11d5994594f` (\"deps: bump pypandoc-binary 1.17, ruff 0.16.2\") states the\nfingerprint was \"darwin-arm64 hashed from the installed binary\" — which is exactly the mechanism\nof the defect. Nothing checked that the installed binary was arm64.\n\n## Why this matters beyond one red test\n\n1. **No genuine arm64 pandoc can ever satisfy the check.** The pinned value is not a real\n   arm64 binary's hash, so any correct remedy for `dc28` deterministically fails this test.\n2. **The darwin-arm64 byte-safety guarantee is vacuous.** The binary whose hash is pinned\n   raises `Bad CPU type in executable` on arm64. Whatever established the frozen conversion\n   outputs for that platform key, it was not an executable that runs there.\n3. It is a false negative masquerading as provenance: the check passes only while the\n   configured pandoc is one that cannot run.\n\n## Decision and evidence (operator, 2026-10-19)\n\nOption (a): accept BOTH fingerprints under `darwin-arm64`. Evidence is in this ticket's comments:\nthe official jgm/pandoc 3.9 release `pandoc-3.9-arm64-macOS.zip` is installed per\n`docs/local-dev-env.md:56-64` at `~/.local/pandoc-3.9/pandoc-3.9-arm64/bin/pandoc` (`file`:\nMach-O 64-bit executable arm64; `--version`: pandoc 3.9; binary sha256\n`140353e19f2518a76aa144ce90a7afcb6f485ba94d0dbe069e77c805277908c3`). With `PYPANDOC_PANDOC`\npointing at it, all 16 fixture-comparison tests in `test_wiki_render_hardening.py` pass, so the\nnative binary reproduces `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` byte for byte; the only\nfailure is this provenance check. The Intel value `d7b1e75c…` stays accepted because it is what\nthe default `pypandoc-binary` wheel installs (it runs under Rosetta).\n\n## Approach\n\n- `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py`: keep `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` unchanged.\n  It is the frozen generating fingerprint map that the committed legacy manifest and the three\n  replay fixtures embed and are compared against, so changing its shape would force regenerating\n  all four fixture files for no behaviour change. Add `ACCEPTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256`, the set of\n  binaries verification accepts per platform: `darwin-arm64` = {Intel `d7b1e75c…`, arm64\n  `140353e1…`}, `linux-x86_64` = {`decd3dd1…`}. The installed-binary comparison at `:149-152`\n  becomes membership in that set, and its error lists the accepted set sorted. The generating-hash\n  check (`:127-132`) uses the same membership, so a future regeneration on a native arm64 host is\n  not refused.\n- `tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py`: one new test asserting both\n  `darwin-arm64` hashes are accepted and a third is rejected with an error naming both accepted\n  hashes; the existing validation tests stay unchanged.\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md:67-72`: drop the \"one test still fails\" paragraph (the defect it\n  describes is fixed); the install instructions above it stay.\n- No fixture file changes (byte identity is proven above).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Both fingerprints are accepted under `darwin-arm64`: the new test passes for the Intel and\n      the arm64 hash, and rejects a third hash with an error that lists both accepted hashes.\n- [ ] Red then green: with `PYPANDOC_PANDOC` set to the native arm64 pandoc,\n      `test_the_installed_pandoc_matches_the_legacy_fixture_provenance` fails before the change and\n      passes after it (both runs recorded on this ticket).\n- [ ] The existing generator validation tests in `tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py`\n      pass unchanged, and `git diff` touches no file under `tests/fixtures/`.\n- [ ] `docs/local-dev-env.md` no longer says a test still fails after the documented setup, and\n      `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` passes.\n- [ ] `make verify` with `PYPANDOC_PANDOC` exported finishes with 0 failures.\n\n## Testing\n\n```\nexport PYPANDOC_PANDOC=$HOME/.local/pandoc-3.9/pandoc-3.9-arm64/bin/pandoc\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py -q\nmake lint && make typecheck && make verify\n```"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792537784843485001,"uuid":"6762a58a-333c-4f6a-9299-6c966b4f6fa9"}